## DESCRIPTION
## Smooth manifolds
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject('Calculus - multivariable')
## DBchapter('Concepts for multivariable functions')
## DBsection('Smooth manifolds')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "PGML.pl", "MathObjects.pl");

TEXT(beginproblem());

$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;

BEGIN_PGML
Let [` S = \lbrace (x,y) \in \mathbb{R}^2: x^2+y^2 = 1 \rbrace `] be the unit circle. Fix [` p = (0,1) \in S `].

For which values of [` \epsilon `] is [` B_{\epsilon}(p) \cap S `] a graph of the form [` y = f(x) `] for a [` C^1 `] function [` f `]? If the answer is none, enter [`(0,0)`].

[` \epsilon \in `] ([________]{Real(0)}, [________]{Compute(sqrt(2))}).

For which values of [` \epsilon `] is [` B_{\epsilon}(p) \cap S `] a graph of the form [` x = f(y) `] for a [` C^1 `] function [` g `]? If the answer is none, enter [`(0,0)`].

[` \epsilon \in `] ([________]{Real(0)}, [________]{Compute(0)}).
END_PGML

ENDDOCUMENT();